    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`copy_with_check` compares `loaded_rank` (an integer) with `torch.float8_e8m0fnu`, so its E8M0-specific destination check never runs. For example, E8M0 scales containing `2**20` and `2**-30` are silently copied to FP16 as `inf` and `0`.\n\n## Modifications\n\nCompare the source and destination tensor dtypes instead. This restores the existing E8M0/FP32 allow-list without changing the ordinary rank-based downcasting policy.\n\nAdd registered CPU tests for allowed destinations, rejection before target mutation (including with the downcasting override), ordinary dtype behavior, and the real `BlockQuantScaleParameter.load_column_parallel_weight` path.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOn the unchanged baseline, the new tests reproduce 15 failing subcases. With the fix, all 4 test methods pass, with no skips:\n\n```bash\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=999 PYTHONPATH=\"$PWD/python\" python test/registered/unit/layers/test_parameter.py\n```\n\nTested on WSL Linux, Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.13.0+cu130, with CUDA hidden. These use real CPU tensors and the production loading code. No full-model accuracy run was performed.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable; this restores a weight-loading validation check. No performance claim.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changed-file pre-commit hooks pass.\n- [x] Registered CPU regression tests added and run.\n- [x] Existing dtype-policy behavior covered.\n- [x] `git diff --check` passes.\n- Documentation: no public API change.\n\nAI assistance was used to develop and validate this change.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35515192814](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35515192814)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35515192701](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35515192701)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35515192817](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35515192817)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
